**`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`** — three hunks:
- `:1245` `cell-ref-shaped-node` — **changed**: id-language discriminator retired; structural shape (type/`:id`/`:seal`, 3 entries, 64-char string seal) kept as the pre-filter for WHEN to ask; docstring rewritten to the ruled semantics.
- `:1403` `compile-guest-call` routing — **changed**: the cell-ref branch emits `(cell/authentic? callee)`; authentic → `admitted` (cell/get + admission/apply), else → `value-call` (map invocation). Entry-key branch untouched.
- `:1458` guard wraps (`yang.call/eligible?`, `invoke`/`invoke-with`) — **changed with zero hunk lines**: they gate through `dsg__admitted?`, whose cell branch now consults `cell/authentic?` before `cell/get`, so a forged candidate answers `false` instead of aborting.

**`src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc` — `:23` `_descriptor`** — **changed**: derefs only when the heap authenticates; an unauthenticated `:cell-ref` shape projects to itself and follows the ordinary descriptor rules (the entry-key policy then governs it as any map). `host-names` grows `cell/authentic?` (flows into the TS/PHP/Python preludes' `admit` sets and the `yang.call` module's free names automatically).

**TS prelude `:135` (typeof path)** — **changed**: `js/cell?` consults authenticity, so `js/symbol?`/`js/object?`/`js/kind-of`/`js/is-array?` never deref an imitation; a forged shape falls to `js/kind-of`'s pre-existing foreign-value fallback (`:number`, the class every foreign map already answers) — no abort, no capability.

**TS lower `:1167` (member-call)** — **documented, unchanged**: the lowering preserves the receiver (`js/get-value` + `js/call f o args`) and routes through `js/call` → `invoke-with` → `_descriptor`, which consults. Residual noted: `js/is-constructor?`'s `(cell/get v)` is guarded by `js/callable?` (= `eligible?`, consulting), so only the entry-carrying exception class (rule 7, out of scope) can reach it.

**Python prelude `:1033` (`py/call-kw`)** — **changed via its two gates, no `py/call-kw` hunk**: `py/cell?` consults (fixing `py/content-type`'s deref everywhere, bound-method and class branches included) and `yang.call/eligible?`/`invoke` consult via `_descriptor`. A forged shape falls to the Python TypeError "object is not callable".

**PHP prelude `:4229` (`php/callable-in`)** — **documented, unchanged**: `php/kind` routes on `:php/*` keys, never `:type :cell-ref`; the entry test goes through `yang.call/entry` → `_descriptor` (consulting); every other `cell/get` on the PHP path derefs PHP's own internal cells (`php.rt/*`, array handles). A forged shape resolves to "Value not callable".

